\mathbf{k}</m>.</p>
<p>a) Find a function <m>f</m> such that <m>\mathbf{F} = \nabla f</m> and 
<m>f(0,0,0) = 0</m>.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y,z) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>b) Suppose C is any curve from <m>\left( 0, 0, 0 \right)</m> to <m>\left( 1, 1, 1 \right).</m> 
Use part a) to compute the line integral <m>\int_{C} \mathbf{F} \cdot d\mathbf{r}</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
